export anchor VelvetTheatreStyle:
    number: 242
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Velvet theatre
    idea:
        The dashboard is staged inside a theatre, with deep red velvet
        curtains and a scalloped pelmet framing a spotlit stage, the figures
        printed on ticket stubs, the projects listed in a gilt programme and
        the chart drawn as arched gilt columns.
    base: dark
    palette:
        house: #120a0b, the page outside the stage and the style sheet
        stage: #1a0e0f, the stage floor behind the content
        spot: #2a1a17, the brightest point of the spotlight, the lightest surface text sits on
        programme: #1f1112, the programme, chart and notices panels
        velvet: #5a0f1a, curtains, the pelmet and ticket stubs
        velvetDeep: #3a0910, curtain fold shadows and the current nav item
        velvetHi: #7a1a28, curtain fold highlights, decoration only
        gilt: #e6c372, programme rules, display type, the primary button, this week columns, links and focus
        giltInk: #2a0d10, text on gilt
        ink: #f5e9d6, body text and figures
        muted: #d1b9a4, meta, labels and axis text
        rose: #e88a9a, last week column outlines
        ok: #a6e0a0, On track text and check circle
        risk: #f4cf6e, At risk text and triangle
        bad: #ff9e93, Behind and overdue text, crossed square and clock
    type:
        Two serif stacks. Display text uses Big Caslon, Goudy Old Style,
        Garamond, Times New Roman, serif, with the greeting 44px, ticket
        figures 40px, section titles 26px in small caps tracked 0.08em and
        programme entries 22px italic. Body text uses Hoefler Text, Garamond,
        Times New Roman, serif at 16px and 1.55, with act numbers and labels
        14px small caps at 600.
    layout:
        A velvet pelmet runs across the top with a scalloped lower edge and a
        gilt fringe line. It holds the Brightwork name centred in gilt display
        type between two small stars, and below it the six nav links in small
        caps with Home on a deeper velvet tab, a search field, a bell, a gilt
        New project button and Mara Okafor at right. Under the pelmet two 88px
        velvet curtains with vertical folds frame the stage, which has a warm
        spotlight from above. On stage the greeting is centred in large gilt
        type with the date and a coral line reading 4 tasks are overdue with a
        clock. The four figures are velvet ticket stubs with notched ends and
        a dashed tear line, each a gilt number and a small caps label, overdue
        with a coral number. Then Tonight's programme, a programme panel with
        a double gilt rule border, lists the six projects as Act I to Act VI
        in two columns of centred entries, each the act number, the italic
        name, the category, a thin gilt meter, the status with its symbol,
        tasks done and due date, with small diamond ornaments between entries.
        Below sit two panels, the chart as paired arched columns by weekday,
        last week as rose outlines and this week solid gilt, and the notices
        of activity as a call board list. Below 900px the curtains shrink to
        16px edges, the programme becomes one column and the panels stack.
    spacing:
        An 8px unit. 32px programme padding, 24px between entries, 40px
        between stage sections.
    density: Low to medium. A staged, ceremonial layout with room to breathe.
    corners: Square panels with arched column tops, notched ticket stubs and a scalloped pelmet.
    borders:
        Double gilt rules on the programme, 1px gilt rules on panels, a dashed
        tear line on each stub.
    shadows:
        The curtains cast deep inner shadows on the stage and a warm spotlight
        falls from above, nothing on the controls.
    icons:
        Thin line icons at 1.6px stroke in gilt. Status uses a check circle, a
        triangle with a bang and a crossed square, always with the word,
        overdue a clock.
    focus: A 2px gilt outline offset 3px.
    tone:
        Ceremonial and playful, such as Tonight's programme, Act I and
        Notices, without overdoing it.
